**Verdict: REJECT** (as a plan ready to implement). Two of the four previous critical defects are fixed. One is fixed in letter but the replacement mechanism does not exist on the path chosen. One is fixed by a substitution that removes the ledger's clock. The revision also introduces one new architectural defect. `plan.md` is the migration plan; `cat.md` is `docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`; `idx.cljc` is `src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc`.

## Status of the four previous critical defects

| Previous defect | Status |
|---|---|
| Missing batch envelope | **Fixed.** S1 carries `{:yin/batch :yin/root …}`; S1 and S2 are separate media; the AST indexer's input predicate is on the envelope (plan.md:23-24, 50, 59). Residual gap in finding 5. |
| Undefined occurrence key | **Partially fixed.** The entity is now `[:yin.occ/origin :yin.occ/root :yin.occ/path]` (plan.md:51). The idempotency mechanism claimed for it does not exist on the chosen ingestion path (finding 1), and the `medium`/`batch` coordinates of `origin` are still unnamed (finding 4). |
| `dao.space.transactor` used for index materialization | **Replaced, and the replacement is a defect.** The index session in `:unresolved` mode never mints `t`, so every writer on S2 chooses its own `t`, which cat.md §8.1 forbids (finding 2). My previous review's recommendation was incomplete on this point. |
| Semantic VM observing raw rows | **Fixed.** VM observes S1, lowers locally, executes the vector (plan.md:54-56). This is exactly cat.md:919-921 (`lower` composed in front, as `linearize/ast-loader`). Residual gap in finding 6. |

